// TNG THEATERS - who a mission fights, and what they look like.
//
// A theater rosters races in the MISSION'S OWN vocabulary (kralien, torgoth, ...) because
// LegendaryMissions BRANCHES on those names: borderwar and deepstrike both run
// `if enemy1 == "Kralien":` to choose an enemy station type. A roster naming Trek factions
// directly would make every one of those branches fall through and the map would spawn no
// enemy stations at all, silently. `Art:` is what says how those races are DRAWN.
//
// ORDER IS DOMINANCE. The map keeps its own weight curve - siege runs [70, 10, 10, 10] at
// difficulty 5 and [10, 30, 30, 30] at 11 - and applies it to this list in order. So the
// FIRST race listed is the one you will mostly be shooting at.
//
// FACTION DEPTH DECIDES WHAT CAN LEAD. The pack ships four hulls each for Cardassian,
// Klingon, Romulan, Kazon and Orion; two for Dominion; and exactly ONE for Breen. A faction
// in the 70% slot with one hull means every enemy that night is the same model, so Breen
// and Dominion only ever appear in the 10% slots below. `theater_depth_report()` enforces
// this and will name the faction if it is ever got wrong.
//
// `usfp`, `tsn` and `civ` are in every `Art:` map even though they are not enemies - they
// re-skin the FRIENDLY side. `usfp` is the one that matters and the one that is easy to miss:
// stock starbases and civilian freighters are side `USFP` in shipData, NOT `tsn`, so a map
// naming only tsn/civ leaves every station and freighter stock. `skaraan` is mapped too even
// though no map rosters it - it still spawns from other paths.

# [Dominion War](dominion_war)
---
Races: kralien, torgoth, arvonian, ximni
Art:   kralien=Cardassian, torgoth=Dominion, arvonian=Breen, ximni=Klingon, skaraan=Dominion, usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: kralien=cardassian, torgoth=jemhadar, arvonian=vorta, ximni=klingon, tsn=human, civ=human
Player Faction: Federation
Music: TNG_Music
---
The Alpha Quadrant at war. Cardassian space is the front line, the Dominion holds the
wormhole, and a Breen raid is the thing nobody is ready for. Matches the Chin'toka and DS9
trials, so it is the theater to run alongside them.

# [Klingon War](klingon_war)
---
Races: kralien, torgoth, arvonian, ximni
Art:   kralien=Klingon, torgoth=Romulan, arvonian=Orion, ximni=Kazon, skaraan=Breen, usfp=Federation, tsn=Federation, civ=Federation
Faces: kralien=klingon, torgoth=romulan, arvonian=orion, ximni=kazon, tsn=human, civ=human
Player Faction: Federation
Music: TNG_Music
---
The alliance has broken. Every faction here has four hulls, which makes this the most varied
theater in the pack - the one to pick if a night should not feel repetitive.

